      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first identify the first term and the common ratio. The first term \\(a\\) is 1, and the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2. The general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series is given by \\(a_n = ar^{n-1}\\). We need to determine the number of terms in the series. The last term is 1024, so we can write:\n\n\\[1024 = 1 \\cdot 2^{n-1} \\implies 2^{n-1} = 1024.\\]\n\nSince \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), we have:\n\n\\[2^{n-1} = 2^{10} \\implies n-1 = 10 \\implies n = 11.\\]\n\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}.\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1.\\]\n\nCalculating \\(2^{11}\\):\n\n\\[2^{11} = 2048.\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum is:\n\n\\[2048 - 1 = 2047.\\]\n\nThe sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{2047}\\).",
